%% Sequence Diagram: Create Product (Admin)
%% Based on Chapter 7 — Detailed Design

sequenceDiagram
    actor Admin
    participant AdminSPA as Admin SPA<br/>(Vue 3)
    participant Carter as Carter Endpoint<br/>(CreateProduct.Endpoint)
    participant Pipeline as MediatR Pipeline
    participant ValBeh as ValidationBehavior
    participant ExcBeh as ExceptionMappingBehavior
    participant Handler as CreateProduct<br/>CommandHandler
    participant Db as ApplicationDbContext<br/>(EF Core)
    participant Sender as ISender<br/>(MediatR)
    participant VariantHandler as AddVariant<br/>CommandHandler

    Admin->>AdminSPA: Fill form + click "Create"
    AdminSPA->>Carter: POST /api/catalog/admin/products<br/>+ JWT Bearer + X-CSRF-TOKEN
    Carter->>Pipeline: sender.Send(new Command(request))
    Pipeline->>ValBeh: Validate(request)
    alt Validation fails
        ValBeh-->>Carter: Result.Validation(errors)
        Carter-->>AdminSPA: 400 Bad Request<br/>{isSuccess:false, errors:[]}
    else Validation passes
        ValBeh->>ExcBeh: Forward to handler
        ExcBeh->>Handler: Handle(Command)
        Handler->>Db: Query: slug exists?
        Db-->>Handler: false
        Handler->>Handler: Product.Create()<br/>factory method
        Handler->>Db: db.Products.Add(product)
        Handler->>Db: SaveChanges()
        Handler->>Sender: Send(new AddVariant.Command(...))
        Sender->>VariantHandler: Dispatch via pipeline
        VariantHandler->>Db: Add variant + set IsMaster
        VariantHandler-->>Sender: Result.Success
        Sender-->>Handler: variantResult
        Handler->>Handler: product.MasterVariantId = variant.Id
        Handler->>Db: SaveChanges()
        Handler-->>ExcBeh: Result<Response>.Created(...)
        ExcBeh-->>Pipeline: result
        Pipeline-->>Carter: result
        Carter-->>AdminSPA: 201 Created<br/>{isSuccess:true, data:{id, name, masterVariantId}}
    end
```

## Diagram Description

This sequence diagram demonstrates the **vertical slice + pipeline** architecture for a representative admin feature. Key design elements visible:

1. **FluentValidation short-circuit** — `ValidationBehavior` stops the pipeline before the handler if rules fail.
2. **Nested command dispatch** — `CreateProduct` dispatches `AddVariant` via `ISender`, demonstrating module-internal CQRS and the MediatR dispatch pattern.
3. **Two SaveChanges calls** — product is saved first (to get its ID), then variant is added and saved. This is a deliberate trade-off for ID generation vs. batching.
4. **Exception mapping** — any unhandled exception in the handler is caught by `ExceptionMappingBehavior` and converted to `Result.Unexpected`.

**Evidence**: `CreateProduct.cs:36-78`, `CreateProduct.Endpoint.cs:14-32`, `Validation.Behavior.cs:1-67`, `Exception.Behavior.cs:1-42`
